module

public import Mathlib.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Presheaf.Abelian
public import Mathlib.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Presheaf.Colimits
public import Mathlib.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Presheaf.Pushforward
public import StacksCore.CategoryTheory.GradedObject.Abelian
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Cech.GenSetCechColimit

/-!
# The complex `K(A, I)` as a complex of presheaves of modules over the rings carrying an ideal

A **ring with an ideal** is a commutative ring `A` together with an ideal `I ⊆ A`; a morphism of
such is a ring map carrying the ideal of the source *onto* the ideal of the target, in the sense
that the target's ideal is the ideal generated by the image. These are the objects
`Stacks.RingIdealSite.RingIdeal`, and on them the filtered colimit of
`StacksFrontier/RingTheory/Cech/GenSetCechColimit.lean` assembles into one **complex of presheaves
of modules**

`K^n(X) = colim_{S ∈ GenSet A I} Č^n(A, fam S)`,   `X = (A, I)`,

with an augmentation onto the structure presheaf in degree zero. Its restriction maps are the
descended transports, which compose on the nose, so this is a presheaf of modules and not merely
a family of complexes with comparisons.

This is the base of the construction of [Stacks, Tag 099E]. That proof attaches to an object `U`
of a ringed site and a finitely generated ideal `I ⊆ 𝒪(U)` generating `ℐ|_U` the complex of
presheaves `K^•_{U, I} : U'/U ↦ K(𝒪(U'), I𝒪(U'))` on the slice site `𝒞/U`, and then has to
compare the complexes obtained from two such ideals `I` and `I'`. The comparison is possible
because both are **pullbacks of the one presheaf of this file** along the two functors
`(𝒞/U)ᵒᵖ ⥤ RingIdeal` sending `U'` to `(𝒪(U'), I𝒪(U'))` and to `(𝒪(U'), I'𝒪(U'))`; those two
functors agree at every object above which the two ideals of sections coincide, which is a
covering sieve of `U` by
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.exists_sieve_sectionSpan_eq`.

The complex of `StacksFrontier/RingTheory/Cech/GenPairSite.lean` is the same construction on the
category `Stacks.GenPairSite.GenPair r` of rings carrying a *chosen family of `r` elements*. That
chosen family is what makes it unusable for the comparison above: two ideals with different
numbers of generators give presheaves on the two different categories `GenPair r` and
`GenPair s`. The value of `K` mentions only the ring and the ideal, never the family, so
forgetting the family loses nothing — which is the content of "`K` depends only on the pair" —
and that is what this file does.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.RingIdealSite.RingIdeal` — the category of rings with an ideal, with
  `Stacks.RingIdealSite.ringFunctor` and `Stacks.RingIdealSite.structureRings` its structure
  presheaf of rings.
* `Stacks.RingIdealSite.RingIdealModule` — presheaves of modules on it, with
  `Stacks.RingIdealSite.evaluation` and `Stacks.RingIdealSite.structureModule`.
* `Stacks.RingIdealSite.kTerm`, `Stacks.RingIdealSite.kDiff`,
  `Stacks.RingIdealSite.kComplexNat` — **the complex of presheaves of modules**, degreewise the
  filtered colimit, and `Stacks.RingIdealSite.kAugZero` its augmentation onto the structure
  presheaf.
* `Stacks.RingIdealSite.sectionsNat`, `Stacks.RingIdealSite.sectionsLegNat` — the complex of
  sections at an object, and the leg of the colimit at one index.
* `Stacks.RingIdealSite.ofIdealAssignment` — a restriction-compatible assignment of ideals over
  a presheaf of commutative rings, read as a functor into the rings with an ideal.

## Main results

* `Stacks.RingIdealSite.isColimit_sectionsCoconeNat` — **the sections at an object are the
  filtered colimit** of the Čech complexes of the product families.
* `Stacks.RingIdealSite.quasiIso_sectionsLegNat` — **each leg of that colimit is a
  quasi-isomorphism** when the ideal is finitely generated: the index system is then filtered and
  all its transitions are quasi-isomorphisms.
* `Stacks.RingIdealSite.comp_ofIdealAssignment_eq` — **two assignments of ideals agreeing above
  a subcategory give the same functor there**, hence the same pullback of the complex: the form in
  which [Stacks, Tag 099E]'s independence of the chosen generators is used, with the two
  restrictions *equal* and not merely isomorphic.

## Implementation notes

The value of a presheaf of modules at `X` is an object of `ModuleCat ↑(structureRings.obj X)`
while every Čech construction produces an object of `ModuleCat X.ring`. The two categories are
definitionally equal but not syntactically so, and `rw`, `simp` and instance search all work
below the transparency at which they become equal; as in
`StacksFrontier/RingTheory/Cech/GenPairSite.lean`, everything below names the `ModuleCat X.ring`
spelling.

No finite-generation condition is imposed on the ideal of an object: the index system
`Stacks.GenFamily.GenSet A I` is empty when `I` is not finitely generated, the colimit is then
the zero module, and nothing below breaks. Finite generation is a hypothesis only where it is
used, namely in `Stacks.RingIdealSite.quasiIso_sectionsLegNat`.

No `@[stacks]` attribute is attached: the complex of this file is the presheaf-level model of
[Stacks, Tag 099D]'s complex, and no clause of a tag is settled by the construction alone.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 099D](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/099D)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 099E](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/099E)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

universe u u₁ v₁ u₂ v₂

namespace Stacks.RingIdealSite

open Stacks.GenFamily

/-! ### The category of rings with an ideal -/

/-- **A ring with an ideal**: a commutative ring together with an ideal of it. -/
structure RingIdeal : Type (u + 1) where
  /-- The underlying ring. -/
  ring : Type u
  /-- Its commutative ring structure. -/
  commRing : CommRing ring
  /-- The ideal. -/
  ideal : Ideal ring

attribute [instance] RingIdeal.commRing

/-- **A morphism of rings with an ideal**: a ring map for which the ideal of the target is the
ideal generated by the image of the ideal of the source. -/
structure RingIdeal.Hom (P Q : RingIdeal.{u}) where
  /-- The underlying ring map. -/
  toRingHom : P.ring →+* Q.ring
  /-- The ideal of the target is generated by the image of the ideal of the source. -/
  map_ideal : Q.ideal = Ideal.map toRingHom P.ideal

/-- A morphism of rings with an ideal is determined by its underlying ring map. -/
theorem RingIdeal.Hom.ext' {P Q : RingIdeal.{u}} :
    ∀ {f g : RingIdeal.Hom P Q}, f.toRingHom = g.toRingHom → f = g
  | ⟨_, _⟩, ⟨_, _⟩, rfl => rfl

/-- **The category of rings with an ideal.** It is locally small: the morphisms between two
objects form a `Type u`. -/
instance : Category.{u, u + 1} RingIdeal.{u} where
  Hom P Q := RingIdeal.Hom P Q
  id P := ⟨RingHom.id P.ring, (Ideal.map_id P.ideal).symm⟩
  comp {_ _ _} f g :=
    ⟨g.toRingHom.comp f.toRingHom, by
      rw [g.map_ideal, f.map_ideal, Ideal.map_map]⟩
  id_comp f := RingIdeal.Hom.ext' (RingHom.comp_id f.toRingHom)
  comp_id f := RingIdeal.Hom.ext' (RingHom.id_comp f.toRingHom)
  assoc f g h := RingIdeal.Hom.ext' (RingHom.comp_assoc f.toRingHom g.toRingHom h.toRingHom).symm

/-- The ring map underlying the identity morphism is the identity. -/
@[simp]
theorem id_toRingHom (P : RingIdeal.{u}) :
    RingIdeal.Hom.toRingHom (𝟙 P) = RingHom.id P.ring := rfl

/-- The ring map underlying a composite is the composite of the ring maps. -/
@[simp]
theorem comp_toRingHom {P Q S : RingIdeal.{u}} (f : P ⟶ Q) (g : Q ⟶ S) :
    (f ≫ g).toRingHom = g.toRingHom.comp f.toRingHom := rfl

/-! ### Functors into the rings with an ideal, from an assignment of ideals -/

section OfIdealAssignment

variable {C : Type u₁} [Category.{v₁} C] (O : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ CommRingCat.{u})

/-- **A restriction-compatible assignment of ideals, read as a functor into the rings with an
ideal.** The datum is an ideal `I U ⊆ O(U)` for every object, such that the ideal at a smaller
object is generated by the image of the ideal at the larger one — exactly the condition a
morphism of `Stacks.RingIdealSite.RingIdeal` asks for.

This is the shape in which the construction of [Stacks, Tag 099E] produces its functor: there `O`
is the structure sheaf of a ringed site and `I U` is the ideal spanned over `U` by the values of
finitely many global sections. -/
def ofIdealAssignment (I : ∀ U : Cᵒᵖ, Ideal (O.obj U))
    (hI : ∀ {U V : Cᵒᵖ} (g : U ⟶ V), I V = Ideal.map (O.map g).hom (I U)) :
    Cᵒᵖ ⥤ RingIdeal.{u} where
  obj U := { ring := O.obj U, commRing := inferInstance, ideal := I U }
  map {_ _} g := { toRingHom := (O.map g).hom, map_ideal := hI g }
  map_id U := RingIdeal.Hom.ext' (congrArg CommRingCat.Hom.hom (O.map_id U))
  map_comp {_ _ _} g h := RingIdeal.Hom.ext' (congrArg CommRingCat.Hom.hom (O.map_comp g h))

/-- The ring of `ofIdealAssignment O I hI` at `U` is `O(U)`. -/
@[simp]
theorem ofIdealAssignment_obj_ring (I : ∀ U : Cᵒᵖ, Ideal (O.obj U))
    (hI : ∀ {U V : Cᵒᵖ} (g : U ⟶ V), I V = Ideal.map (O.map g).hom (I U)) (U : Cᵒᵖ) :
    ((ofIdealAssignment O I hI).obj U).ring = O.obj U := rfl

/-- The ideal of `ofIdealAssignment O I hI` at `U` is `I U`. -/
@[simp]
theorem ofIdealAssignment_obj_ideal (I : ∀ U : Cᵒᵖ, Ideal (O.obj U))
    (hI : ∀ {U V : Cᵒᵖ} (g : U ⟶ V), I V = Ideal.map (O.map g).hom (I U)) (U : Cᵒᵖ) :
    ((ofIdealAssignment O I hI).obj U).ideal = I U := rfl

/-- The ring map of `ofIdealAssignment O I hI` along `g` is the restriction map `O.map g`. -/
@[simp]
theorem ofIdealAssignment_map_toRingHom (I : ∀ U : Cᵒᵖ, Ideal (O.obj U))
    (hI : ∀ {U V : Cᵒᵖ} (g : U ⟶ V), I V = Ideal.map (O.map g).hom (I U)) {U V : Cᵒᵖ}
    (g : U ⟶ V) :
    ((ofIdealAssignment O I hI).map g).toRingHom = (O.map g).hom := rfl

/-- **The functor depends on the assignment of ideals alone**, the compatibility being a
proposition. -/
theorem ofIdealAssignment_congr {I J : ∀ U : Cᵒᵖ, Ideal (O.obj U)}
    (hI : ∀ {U V : Cᵒᵖ} (g : U ⟶ V), I V = Ideal.map (O.map g).hom (I U))
    (hJ : ∀ {U V : Cᵒᵖ} (g : U ⟶ V), J V = Ideal.map (O.map g).hom (J U)) (h : I = J) :
    ofIdealAssignment O I hI = ofIdealAssignment O J hJ := by
  subst h
  rfl

variable {D : Type u₂} [Category.{v₂} D] (ι : D ⥤ C)

/-- **Restricting the functor along a functor of sites is again a functor of this shape**, for
the restricted presheaf of rings and the restricted assignment of ideals. -/
theorem comp_ofIdealAssignment (I : ∀ U : Cᵒᵖ, Ideal (O.obj U))
    (hI : ∀ {U V : Cᵒᵖ} (g : U ⟶ V), I V = Ideal.map (O.map g).hom (I U)) :
    ι.op ⋙ ofIdealAssignment O I hI =
      ofIdealAssignment (ι.op ⋙ O) (fun d ↦ I (ι.op.obj d))
        (fun {_ _} φ ↦ hI (ι.op.map φ)) := rfl

/-- **Two assignments of ideals agreeing above a subcategory give the same functor there.** This
is the form the independence of [Stacks, Tag 099E]'s complex from the chosen generators takes: the
two restrictions are *equal*, not merely isomorphic. -/
theorem comp_ofIdealAssignment_eq {I J : ∀ U : Cᵒᵖ, Ideal (O.obj U)}
    (hI : ∀ {U V : Cᵒᵖ} (g : U ⟶ V), I V = Ideal.map (O.map g).hom (I U))
    (hJ : ∀ {U V : Cᵒᵖ} (g : U ⟶ V), J V = Ideal.map (O.map g).hom (J U))
    (h : ∀ d : Dᵒᵖ, I (ι.op.obj d) = J (ι.op.obj d)) :
    ι.op ⋙ ofIdealAssignment O I hI = ι.op ⋙ ofIdealAssignment O J hJ :=
  ((comp_ofIdealAssignment O ι I hI).trans
      (ofIdealAssignment_congr (ι.op ⋙ O) _ _ (funext h))).trans
    (comp_ofIdealAssignment O ι J hJ).symm

end OfIdealAssignment

/-! ### The structure presheaf of rings -/

/-- An object of the category of rings with an ideal, read as an index for the values of a
presheaf on the site `RingIdealᵒᵖ`, so that presheaves on it are indexed by `RingIdealᵒᵖᵒᵖ`. -/
abbrev RingIdeal.ix (P : RingIdeal.{u}) : RingIdeal.{u}ᵒᵖᵒᵖ := op (op P)

/-- A morphism of rings with an ideal, read as a morphism of indices for a presheaf. It goes the
same way: a presheaf on `RingIdealᵒᵖ` is a *covariant* functor on rings with an ideal. -/
abbrev RingIdeal.Hom.ix {P Q : RingIdeal.{u}} (f : P ⟶ Q) : P.ix ⟶ Q.ix := (Quiver.Hom.op f).op

/-- **The ring of a ring with an ideal, functorially.** -/
def ringFunctor : RingIdeal.{u} ⥤ RingCat.{u} where
  obj P := RingCat.of P.ring
  map f := RingCat.ofHom f.toRingHom
  map_id _ := rfl
  map_comp _ _ := rfl

/-- **The structure presheaf of rings on the site of rings with an ideal**, in the form Mathlib's
`PresheafOfModules` consumes. -/
def structureRings : RingIdeal.{u}ᵒᵖᵒᵖ ⥤ RingCat.{u} :=
  unopUnop RingIdeal.{u} ⋙ ringFunctor.{u}

/-- The value of `structureRings` at a ring with an ideal is its ring. -/
@[simp]
theorem structureRings_obj (P : RingIdeal.{u}) :
    structureRings.{u}.obj P.ix = RingCat.of P.ring := rfl

/-- The ring map of `structureRings` along a morphism is its underlying ring map. -/
@[simp]
theorem structureRings_map {P Q : RingIdeal.{u}} (f : P ⟶ Q) :
    (structureRings.{u}.map (RingIdeal.Hom.ix f)).hom = f.toRingHom := rfl

/-! ### Presheaves of modules on the site of rings with an ideal -/

/-- **A presheaf of modules on the category of rings with an ideal.** -/
abbrev RingIdealModule := PresheafOfModules.{u} structureRings.{u}

/-- The value of a presheaf of modules on rings with an ideal at an object. -/
abbrev RingIdealModule.value (M : RingIdealModule.{u}) (P : RingIdeal.{u}) :
    ModuleCat.{u} P.ring :=
  M.obj P.ix

/-- **Evaluation at a ring with an ideal.** -/
abbrev evaluation (P : RingIdeal.{u}) : RingIdealModule.{u} ⥤ ModuleCat.{u} P.ring :=
  PresheafOfModules.evaluation structureRings.{u} P.ix

/-- Evaluation at a ring with an ideal is additive. This is `PresheafOfModules.evaluation`'s own
instance, restated with the target written as `ModuleCat P.ring` rather than as
`ModuleCat ↑(structureRings.obj P.ix)`. -/
instance instAdditiveEvaluation (P : RingIdeal.{u}) : (evaluation.{u} P).Additive :=
  inferInstanceAs ((PresheafOfModules.evaluation structureRings.{u} P.ix).Additive)

/-- Evaluation at a ring with an ideal preserves zero morphisms. -/
instance instPreservesZeroMorphismsEvaluation (P : RingIdeal.{u}) :
    (evaluation.{u} P).PreservesZeroMorphisms :=
  Functor.preservesZeroMorphisms_of_additive _

/-- **The structure presheaf, as a presheaf of modules over itself.** -/
abbrev structureModule : RingIdealModule.{u} :=
  PresheafOfModules.unit structureRings.{u}

/-! ### The complex of presheaves of modules -/

/-- **The degree-`n` term of the complex of presheaves of modules**: at the object `X` the
filtered colimit, over the finite sets of finite generating families of the ideal of `X`, of the
degree-`n` Čech terms of their product families. -/
def kTerm (n : ℕ) : RingIdealModule.{u} where
  obj X := (colimit (GenSetCech.cechTermDiagram (X.unop.unop).ring (X.unop.unop).ideal n) :
    ModuleCat.{u} (X.unop.unop).ring)
  map {_ _} f :=
    GenSetCech.transportDesc (RingIdeal.Hom.toRingHom f.unop.unop)
      (RingIdeal.Hom.map_ideal f.unop.unop) n
  map_id X := GenSetCech.transportDesc_id (RingIdeal.Hom.map_ideal (𝟙 (X.unop.unop))) n
  map_comp {_ _ _} f g :=
    GenSetCech.transportDesc_comp (RingIdeal.Hom.toRingHom f.unop.unop)
      (RingIdeal.Hom.toRingHom g.unop.unop) (RingIdeal.Hom.map_ideal f.unop.unop)
      (RingIdeal.Hom.map_ideal g.unop.unop)
      (RingIdeal.Hom.map_ideal (f.unop.unop ≫ g.unop.unop)) n

/-- The value of `kTerm n` at `X` is the colimit of the degree-`n` Čech terms. -/
@[simp]
theorem kTerm_obj (n : ℕ) (X : RingIdeal.{u}ᵒᵖᵒᵖ) :
    (kTerm.{u} n).obj X =
      colimit (GenSetCech.cechTermDiagram (X.unop.unop).ring (X.unop.unop).ideal n) := rfl

/-- The restriction map of `kTerm n` along `f` is `GenSetCech.transportDesc`. -/
@[simp]
theorem kTerm_map (n : ℕ) {X Y : RingIdeal.{u}ᵒᵖᵒᵖ} (f : X ⟶ Y) :
    (kTerm.{u} n).map f =
      GenSetCech.transportDesc (RingIdeal.Hom.toRingHom f.unop.unop)
        (RingIdeal.Hom.map_ideal f.unop.unop) n := rfl

/-- **The differential of the complex of presheaves of modules.** -/
def kDiff (n : ℕ) : kTerm.{u} n ⟶ kTerm.{u} (n + 1) where
  app X := GenSetCech.diffDesc (X.unop.unop).ring (X.unop.unop).ideal n
  naturality {_ _} f :=
    GenSetCech.transportDesc_comp_diffDesc (RingIdeal.Hom.toRingHom f.unop.unop)
      (RingIdeal.Hom.map_ideal f.unop.unop) n

/-- The component of `kDiff n` at `X` is `GenSetCech.diffDesc`. -/
@[simp]
theorem kDiff_app (n : ℕ) (X : RingIdeal.{u}ᵒᵖᵒᵖ) :
    PresheafOfModules.Hom.app (kDiff.{u} n) X =
      GenSetCech.diffDesc (X.unop.unop).ring (X.unop.unop).ideal n := rfl

/-- **The complex of presheaves of modules of [Stacks, Tag 099D], in nonnegative degrees.** -/
def kComplexNat : CochainComplex RingIdealModule.{u} ℕ :=
  CochainComplex.of kTerm.{u} kDiff.{u} fun n =>
    PresheafOfModules.hom_ext fun X =>
      GenSetCech.diffDesc_comp_diffDesc (A := (X.unop.unop).ring)
        (I := (X.unop.unop).ideal) n

/-- The degree-`n` term of `kComplexNat` is `kTerm n`. -/
@[simp]
theorem kComplexNat_X (n : ℕ) : kComplexNat.{u}.X n = kTerm.{u} n := rfl

/-- The differential of `kComplexNat` from degree `n` to `n + 1` is `kDiff n`. -/
@[simp]
theorem kComplexNat_d (n : ℕ) : kComplexNat.{u}.d n (n + 1) = kDiff.{u} n :=
  CochainComplex.of_d _ _ n

/-- **The augmentation of the degree-zero term onto the structure presheaf.** -/
def kAugZero : kTerm.{u} 0 ⟶ structureModule.{u} where
  app X := GenSetCech.augDesc (X.unop.unop).ring (X.unop.unop).ideal
  naturality {_ _} f :=
    GenSetCech.transportDesc_comp_augDesc (RingIdeal.Hom.toRingHom f.unop.unop)
      (RingIdeal.Hom.map_ideal f.unop.unop)

/-- The component of `kAugZero` at `X` is `GenSetCech.augDesc`. -/
@[simp]
theorem kAugZero_app (X : RingIdeal.{u}ᵒᵖᵒᵖ) :
    PresheafOfModules.Hom.app kAugZero.{u} X =
      GenSetCech.augDesc (X.unop.unop).ring (X.unop.unop).ideal := rfl

/-! ### The sections at an object are the filtered colimit -/

/-- **The complex of sections of the complex of presheaves of modules at an object**, written
over the object's own ring. -/
abbrev sectionsNat (P : RingIdeal.{u}) : CochainComplex (ModuleCat.{u} P.ring) ℕ :=
  ((evaluation P).mapHomologicalComplex (ComplexShape.up ℕ)).obj kComplexNat.{u}

/-- The differential of `sectionsNat P` from degree `n` to `n + 1` is `GenSetCech.diffDesc`. -/
theorem sectionsNat_d (P : RingIdeal.{u}) (n : ℕ) :
    (sectionsNat P).d n (n + 1) = GenSetCech.diffDesc P.ring P.ideal n :=
  congrArg (fun w => (evaluation P).map w) (kComplexNat_d.{u} n)

/-- **The sections at an object, as a cocone** on the filtered diagram of Čech complexes. -/
def sectionsCoconeNat (P : RingIdeal.{u}) :
    Cocone (GenSetCech.cechDiagram P.ring P.ideal) where
  pt := sectionsNat P
  ι :=
    { app := fun S =>
        { f := fun n => colimit.ι (GenSetCech.cechTermDiagram P.ring P.ideal n) S
          comm' := fun n m hnm => by
            obtain rfl : n + 1 = m := hnm
            exact Eq.trans (congrArg
              (fun w => colimit.ι (GenSetCech.cechTermDiagram P.ring P.ideal n) S ≫ w)
              (sectionsNat_d P n)) (GenSetCech.ι_diffDesc n S) }
      naturality := fun S T h =>
        HomologicalComplex.hom_ext _ _ fun n =>
          (colimit.w (GenSetCech.cechTermDiagram P.ring P.ideal n) h).trans
            (Category.comp_id _).symm }

/-- **The leg of the sections cocone at one generating index**, with its target written as
`Stacks.RingIdealSite.sectionsNat` rather than as the value at `S` of a constant functor. -/
def sectionsLegNat (P : RingIdeal.{u}) (S : GenSet P.ring P.ideal) :
    Cech.cechComplex (fam S) P.ring ⟶ sectionsNat P :=
  (sectionsCoconeNat P).ι.app S

/-- The degree-`n` component of `sectionsLegNat P S` is the colimit injection at `S`. -/
@[simp]
theorem sectionsLegNat_f (P : RingIdeal.{u}) (S : GenSet P.ring P.ideal) (n : ℕ) :
    (sectionsLegNat P S).f n =
      colimit.ι (GenSetCech.cechTermDiagram P.ring P.ideal n) S := rfl

/-- **The sections at an object are the colimit of the filtered diagram.** -/
def isColimit_sectionsCoconeNat (P : RingIdeal.{u}) : IsColimit (sectionsCoconeNat P) := by
  refine HomologicalComplex.isColimitOfEval _ _ fun n => ?_
  exact IsColimit.ofIsoColimit
    (colimit.isColimit (GenSetCech.cechTermDiagram P.ring P.ideal n))
    (Cocone.ext (Iso.refl _) fun S => Category.comp_id _)

/-- **Each leg of the colimit is a quasi-isomorphism** when the ideal is finitely generated. The
index system is then filtered and every transition of the diagram is a quasi-isomorphism. -/
theorem quasiIso_sectionsLegNat (P : RingIdeal.{u}) (hI : P.ideal.FG)
    (S : GenSet P.ring P.ideal) :
    QuasiIso (sectionsLegNat P S) :=
  have := GenSet.isFiltered hI
  StacksDraft.quasiIso_isColimit_ι (GenSetCech.cechDiagram P.ring P.ideal)
    (fun _ _ h => GenSetCech.quasiIso_cechDiagram_map h) (sectionsCoconeNat P)
    (isColimit_sectionsCoconeNat P) S

end Stacks.RingIdealSite

end
